# Provider-Neutral Adapter Wall

- Keep provider SDKs behind runtime adapters only (for example `runtime/openai_*`, `runtime/*_adapter*`).
- Treat OpenAI Agents SDK as a first-class adapter, not orchestration core.
- Core layers (`core`, `tools`, `policies`, `persistence`, `observability`) must depend on internal contracts only.
- Do not import provider SDK types/classes/functions in core layers.
- Execution mode selection must be capability + policy driven, never provider-name hardcoded.
- Force deterministic tool runtime for state-changing, high-risk, or policy-flagged operations.
- Allow provider-native fast path only for low-risk operations when capability and policy gates both pass.

## Required Contracts

- Runtime contract: `start_session`, `run_turn`, `submit_tool_results`, `get_capabilities`, `healthcheck`.
- Tool effects contract: model emits intent, deterministic runtime executes side effects.
- Policy contract: pre-check, post-check, and output checks wrap every side-effect path.

## Enforcement Checklist

- No provider SDK import appears outside adapter modules.
- Removing one provider adapter does not break core orchestration compilation/import graph.
- Same workflow contract executes across at least two adapters.
- Risky tool calls are blocked or rerouted when deterministic mode is required.
